    "explanation": "To both parties, on trip TRP-02801.\n\nThe route deviation is established. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02801) records 26.44 km driven, and the platform's optimal route on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02801) is 21.0 km. The excess is 5.44 km, which is 25.90% of the optimal distance. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass — the excess is above 20% of optimal and above 0.8 km — so the deviation stands. Under POL-RD-01 the trace figure governs over the trip record's rounded 26.4 km; both advocates agree on this and I accept it.\n\nThe deviation is not a material one: 25.90% is below the 50% gate and 5.44 km is below the 8.0 km gate, so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not triggered by materiality. In any event the driver profile (EV-DPROF-02801) shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 against completed_trips_90d of 191, so no repeat pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift follows and no driver-conduct referral is produced. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter mentioned in argument is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used either way.\n\nThe driver's explanation that traffic was heavy and he took another road does not reduce or excuse the deviation. No traffic advisory covers this trip: the only advisory artifact in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02801-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run and the assertion is tested against nothing. An uncited traffic assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and under POL-RD-13 it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. I have also checked that this absence is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction, so it does not escalate the case. Separately, the chat log (EV-CHAT-02801) is empty, so there is no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 and nothing to exclude on that ground; no pickup or dropoff relocation applies under POL-RD-05; and the trip was not pooled (vehicle_type RYDE_X), so no matched-itinerary baseline displaces the 21.0 km optimal.\n\nThe fare is metered, so POL-RD-02 governs (POL-RD-11 does not apply, as quoted_fare_sgd is null). The figures I used are: charged_total SGD 40.71; recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 × 21.0 optimal km + 0.28 × 28.4 optimal min) × 1.2 surge) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 33.8024; refund = 40.71 − 33.8024 = SGD 6.9076, rounded up to SGD 6.95. The surge multiplier of 1.2 was read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, the only artifact carrying it. The refund exceeds the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and is about 17% of the charge, well below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a partial refund.\n\nThere are no ERP gantries or surcharges to correct under POL-RD-09 (the fare breakdown carries none), so nothing is added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. No clause produces a referral in this case. The quantum reflects no unbilled distance either — the fare breakdown billed 26.4 km against the trace's 26.44 km, a shortfall far below 1.0 km — so no driver compensation arises.\n\nMy confidence is 0.90. The deciding facts are carried by artifacts at full weight 1.0 (GPS trace, trip record, fare breakdown), so the POL-GEN-02 cap is 1.0 and the case is well above the 0.70 floor. The only impaired artifact is the missing advisory (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), on which no finding rests.\n\nThe monetary effect, SGD 6.95, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it is executed automatically. Both parties may appeal this provisional ruling once within 30 days.",
